# Task breakdown teaching example 0.1

This English example follows the task refinement supplement dated 2026-10-08. Its inputs, revisions, tasks, and plans are fictional. Confirmation, application execution, project files, tests, and scores remain unobserved. Locate or plan actual paths before using the structure in a real project. Use the locale-matched task packet and the current workflow. [Chinese export](任务细化/任务拆分示例.md), [provenance](任务细化/任务拆分示例.provenance.json), and [English task packet](../assets/task-packet.en-us.md)

## 1. Local saving from requirement to assignable tasks

### 1.1 Fictional input and scope

Project `DEMO-save` uses requirement input `SRC-save@input-v1` and planning draft `PLAN-save@draft-v1`.

| Requirement and revision | Original behavior in this example | Product assertion |
| --- | --- | --- |
| R-save-01@input-v1 | Save a record. After success feedback, normal close and reopen reads the same content. | AC-save-01. Save → success feedback → normal restart → read. Fields agree. |
| R-save-02@input-v1 | If saving fails, report failure, retain input, and preserve earlier saved content. | AC-save-02. After a controlled save failure, input and earlier data remain, and failure is recognizable. |
| R-save-03@input-v1 | Repeating the same save operation preserves a single record. | AC-save-03. Resubmitting one operation ID leaves exactly one matching record. |

`PLAT-demo` is an unverified platform placeholder. Stack, storage, code location, testing tools, fees, and abnormal shutdown or power-loss guarantees are unknown. The requirement concerns normal close and reopen. Obtain a user decision if feasibility affects scope, signing, permissions, or storage guarantees.

All cards cover R-save-01–03. Accounts, networking, cloud sync, export, and other features are outside scope. Each card binds SRC-save@input-v1 and PLAN-save@draft-v1. Read, development, and run permissions are unrecorded. All planned actions remain unexecuted and lack an actual build, test environment, or completion evidence.

