**STEP-decision-save-02.** Bind the actual response to its original wording and revision, then assess confirmation impact. The expected result is an effective decision record or a renewed confirmation gap. Keep unanswered decisions pending.

## 2. Product SOP generation as document work

### 2.1 Fictional input

Project `DEMO-doc` uses `SRC-doc@input-v1`: “Design a local record app for one person. Let them add a record and retain their input when saving fails. Start with a Product SOP draft. Leave technology selection and coding for later.” Fields, ordering, editing, and deletion are unspecified. The fictional target is one Product SOP draft with its actual confirmation state.

Deliverable `B-doc@draft-v1` covers `R-doc-01` add, `R-doc-02` retain input on failure, `R-doc-03` local single-user scope, and `R-doc-04` draft-only delivery. `N-doc@rule-snapshot-v1` is a teaching identifier for the Product fields and PC rules. A real project needs verified source locations.

All cards cover the requested draft and document review. Deletion, cloud sync, login, changes to requirements or decisions, app execution, paid calls, and user research are outside scope. Each card binds SRC-doc@input-v1, B-doc@draft-v1, and N-doc@rule-snapshot-v1. Locations are planned, actual read scope, permission, directory, and actor remain unverified, and every task is unexecuted. The draft owner integrates changes serially. Other executors can propose nonconflicting sections.

