## 3. Example review and boundaries

The cards demonstrate refinement. Their actions remain unexecuted and required prerequisites unknown. The TASK01–10 mapping is a design example. Actual review needs current inputs, permission, locations, and appropriate evidence.

- Local saving separates discovery, contract, implementation, integration, and full-flow verification. Focused checks accompany each implementation. Keep all three original acceptance criteria, including unrun cases, in the integration denominator.
- Document generation separates input scope, behavior, acceptance and technical handoff, and assembly and review. Keep undecided fields open for actual decisions.
- Before a stack is selected, detailed planning can be reviewed and dependent implementation remains blocked. Record permission, confirmation, and test results only from their actual sources.
- Record longer-term ideas at summary and trigger level. Break down future login, sync, migration, or other development only when the project adopts it.
